ar0822-rpi-dkms (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Soft reset sensor to register defaults at stream start. Supports
    camera modules without a wired hardware reset.
  * Convert format, crop and blanking to V4L2 subdev state model.
    TRY state is seeded on open and reports real mode geometry rather
    than zeros.
  * Report 12-bit while wide dynamic range control is on. HDR streams
    are 12-bit only, so a 10-bit request no longer leaves a mismatched
    serial configuration.
  * Report package version through module version field, so modinfo
    and dkms status agree.
  * Build overlay in a temporary directory during DKMS post install,
    leaving no stray build tree behind.
  * Add device-tree-compiler dependency since post install builds
    overlay with dtc.
  * d/rules: Name both remedies in version drift error.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:21:52 +0300

ar0822-rpi-dkms (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report V4L2_COLORSPACE_RAW rather than sRGB. Sensor emits
    unprocessed Bayer, so derived fields follow and xfer_func becomes
    NONE.
  * Handle read-only HBLANK control. Line length ships with mode
    registers, so there is nothing to program. Probe and every mode
    change no longer log an unhandled control.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:35:02 +0300

ar0822-rpi-dkms (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release as a DKMS source package.
  * Driver state at this release:
    - 3840x2160 at up to 40 fps (full resolution), 1920x1080 at up
      to 120 fps (2x2 binning), 10-bit and 12-bit RAW output.
    - 2-lane and 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 at up to 960 Mbps per lane.
    - Experimental eHDR mode (three-exposure on-sensor HDR, companded
      to 12-bit) via the standard V4L2 wide dynamic range control.
    - ar0822 device tree overlay with cam0 and 4lane options.
    - Targeting Linux kernel 6.12 or newer.
    - Validated on Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm
      and Trixie.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Thu, 02 Jul 2026 15:02:03 +0300
